<% content_for :title, "About — Pharma Transport" %>
<% content_for :meta_description, "Pharma Transport is built by Thomas Information Technology in Phoenix, Arizona, to give pharmaceutical transport a real chain-of-custody record instead of reconstructed paperwork." %>

<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-10">
  <div class="text-center space-y-2">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900">About Pharma Transport</h1>
  </div>

  <section class="space-y-3">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">What we do</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-700">
      Pharmaceutical transport generates a lot of paperwork that only gets looked at when
      something goes wrong — a temperature excursion, a missing signature, a regulator asking
      for a record that's supposed to exist. Pharma Transport exists to make that record real
      from the start: GPS tracking, custody handoffs, and signatures logged as they happen, and
      turned into FDA-ready documentation automatically instead of reconstructed from memory
      after the fact.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-3">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">Who's behind this</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-700">
      Pharma Transport is built by <strong>Brett Thomas</strong> through Thomas Information
      Technology, based in Phoenix, Arizona. Brett was born and raised in Arizona, with an IT
      background and an education in Maricopa County — this is a solo-founder, hands-on build:
      the product, the compliance documentation, and the infrastructure it runs on are all
      built and maintained directly, not outsourced.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-3">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">Where things stand</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-700">
      This is an early-stage product: live in production, with real signup, real billing, and a
      real security posture — built to be trusted with the kind of documentation pharmaceutical
      transport actually needs, not a demo. If you want more detail on where things stand or
      how it works, <%= link_to "get in touch", new_user_registration_path, class: "text-brand-700 underline" %>.
    </p>
  </section>
</div>
